cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use dejafix in research or writing, please cite it as below.
title: "dejafix"
type: software
abstract: >-
  dejafix is a local-first memory and judgment layer for AI coding agents. It
  records issues, attempts, fixes, decisions and notes as typed events in plain
  text, serves them to agents through a native MCP server, warns before an
  approach that already failed is repeated, and keeps library lessons in a
  global memory that agents query by relevance.
authors:
  - name: dejafix contributors
version: 1.0.0-rc.3
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bigfree/dejafix"
url: "https://github.com/bigfree/dejafix"
keywords:
  - coding agent memory
  - memory for AI coding agents
  - AI coding agents
  - model context protocol
  - local-first
